        "content": "<p>The King of Love.</p><p>The King of Love my Shepherd is Whose goodness fails never, I nothing lack if I am His And He is mine forever.</p><p>Where streams of living waters flow, My ransomed soul He leads, And where the verdant pastures grow With food celestial feeds</p><p>God is Love and God is Light</p><p>God is Love, His mercy brightens All the path in which we rove, Bliss He forms, and woe He lightens, God is Light and God is Love</p><p>Chance and change are busy ever, Worlds decay and ages move, But His mercy wanes never God is Light and God is Love.</p><p>Your eyes shall see the King</p><p>Your eyes shall see! Yes, your, who, blind erewhile, Now trembling towards the new-found light do flee, Leave doubting, and look up with trustful smile. Your eyes shall see!</p><p>Your eyes shall see the King! The very same Whose love shone forth upon the curseful tree, Who bore your guilt, who calls you by name Your eyes shall see!</p><p>Your eyes shall see the King, the Mighty One, The many crowned, the light-enrobed, and He Shall bid you share the kingdom He has won Your eyes shall see!</p><p>I am Your.</p><p>Jesus Master! I am Your, Keep me faithful keep me near, Let Your presence in me shine All my homeward way to cheer, Jesus! at Your feet I fall, Oh, be You my all in all</p>",
