        "title": "My King and Master",
        "content": "<p>My King and Master.</p><p>Christ my King, my Master, let my whole life be, Spent in blessed service only until You Let me serve You gladly, That the world may know 'Tis a happy privilege, You to serve below.</p><p>Let me serve You humbly, Yours be all the praise, 'Tis Your love alone which tunes my feeble lays; Let me serve You quickly--Time will soon be o'er I would gladly lead many to heaven's peaceful shore.</p><p>Let me serve You ever, from morning until eve, My earliest and my latest breath, my King, You will receive. And oh when service here is spent, and Heaven is won Grant that I too, dear Master, may hear Your sweet \"Well done!\"</p><p>Cecilia Havergal</p>",
